{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-84c099d87baef07b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"State confirmed: no package.json, no test directory. Fresh work needed.\n\nNext, launch the planner sub-agent. In the previous run, the planner had already completed its investigation before being killed. This time I'll relaunch the planner with the same well-scoped prompt. Per the contract: Agent(prompt=\"<agent file contents + task>\"), no model, no subagent_type, no run_in_background.\n\nNote the contract says don't set run_in_background. Launch in the default mode and wait via TaskOutput block:true.\n\nI need to pass the full contents of the agent file. That's long, but necessary. I'll compose the prompt: the body of ecc-planner.md (excluding frontmatter? The contract says \"ENTIRE content of the agent file\". Include everything from the beginning; including the frontmatter is harmless but it's metadata — I'll include the file contents, which is the file body. Actually \"ENTIRE content\" — to be safe I'll include the frontmatter too).\n\nKeep the task section concise — the previous prompt was good and thorough. Reuse it but make it concise since the investigation is done (I can provide facts: npm registry reachable, node:test available, apps/ absent, git remote origin present, untracked noise files). This reduces the time the planner takes.\n","signature":"8ac666e12de64e0e9ab62bd03a0e8fb8"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66996,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b7cff-f541-40f9-ab74-f5dd04029f47","uuid":"0bc89688-bcdf-4480-8352-03ee8b9b17f8","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:59:13.207Z"}
