 the TAP output.\n- Why: TDD — the spec must fail first; the failure mode (ENOENT / \"Cannot find module ../package.json\") proves the test actually exercises the deliverable.\n- Dependencies: none.\n- Risk: reading a missing JSON via `require` throws at load time before tests register — mitigated by doing the `fs.readFileSync` + `JSON.parse` inside the first test body (so a missing file yields a clean test failure, not a crash with zero tests run).\n- Verify: `node --test test/` → **fails** (expected RED, e.g. ENOENT for `package.json`).\n\n### Phase 2 — GREEN\n\n**Step 2: Create `package.json`**\n- Action: Write exactly:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nextmove\",\n    \"private\": true,\n    \"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\"],\n    \"packageManager\": \"npm@10\",\n    \"engines\": { \"node\": \"22.x\" },\n    \"devDependencies\": { \"turbo\": \"^2.5.0\" },\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"build\": \"turbo run build\",\n      \"test\": \"turbo run test\",\n      \"lint\": \"turbo run lint\"\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n- Why: Minimal manifest satisfying ACs 1–3 with no invented extras (no `description`/`homepage`/`type` — nothing requires them, and `\"type\": \"module\"` could break the `.cjs`-assumed test tooling in sibling stories).\n- Dependencies: Step 1.\n- Risk: none — static content.\n- Verify: `node --test test/` → **all 4 tests pass** (GREEN).\n\n**Step 3: Install dependencies and lock**\n- Action: Append `node_modules/` to `.gitignore`, then run `npm install` from the repo root.\n- Why: Validates the manifest resolves against the real registry, creates `package-lock.json`, and proves turbo 2.x resolves (lockfile will show `turbo@2.10.x`).\n- Dependencies: Step 2.\n- Risk: transient npm network failure → re-run; the story states the registry is verified reachable.\n- Verify: `npm ls turbo` → `turbo@2.10.x` (2.x line); `node --test test/` still green; `git status` shows no `node_modules/` (gitignored).\n\n### Phase 3 — Commit & push (AC 4)\n\n**Step 4: Scoped commit**\n- Action:\n  1. `git add package.json test/ package-lock.json .gitignore`\n  2. `git commit -m \"chore: add root package.json with npm workspaces, npm@10, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x, and turbo-run scripts\"`\n  3. `git push origin HEAD 2>/dev/null || true`\n- Why: Each command must exit 0; scoped add guarantees `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph.log`, and `.story-updates/` are excluded. Push with `|| true` tolerates an offline environment per the CLAUDE.md Phase 5 convention.\n- Dependencies: Steps 2–3.\n- Risk: push rejected if remote advanced → `git pull --rebase origin iotahub/phase-1` then re-push; rebase is safe because the commit is brand-new and local-only.\n- Verify: `git status --porcelain` → only the 4 pre-existing untracked noise entries remain; `git log -1 --stat` shows exactly 4 files (`package.json`, `test/package.test.cjs`, `package-lock.json`, `.gitignore`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- **Unit (required by gate — \"pure config, scaffold\" story):** `test/package.test.cjs` via `node --test test/`. 4 tests: JSON-parses precondition + AC 1 + AC 2 + AC 3, each labeled by AC number. Zero dependencies; no framework added.\n- **Integration / E2E:** not required — no runtime logic, no UI. Playwright explicitly out of scope per the Test Strategy Gate.\n- **Deliberate deviation (documented):** root `\"test\"` script remains `turbo run test` (AC 3), so verification invokes the sample test directly with `node --test test/` rather than `npm test`. Recorded here per the gate's deviation rule.\n\n## Verification commands (expected output)\n\n1. `node --test test/` after Step 1 → exit 1, tests fail with ENOENT (RED).\n2. `node --test test/` after Step 2 → `# pass 4` / `# fail 0` (GREEN).\n3. `npm install` → `added N packages` (N ≥ 1, includes turbo).\n4. `npm ls turbo --depth=0` → `turbo@2.10.x` (matches 2.x).\n5. `git log -1 --stat` → 4 files; `git status --porcelain` → only `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph.log` untracked (AC 4: nothing else leaked).\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Accidental commit of untracked noise via `git add -A` | Plan mandates scoped `git add` of the 4 files only; Step 4 verification greps `git status` before push. |\n| Test harness crash instead of clean RED (missing JSON at require time) | Test uses `fs.readFileSync` + `JSON.parse` inside the test body, not top-level `require`. |\n| npm registry flake during install | Registry verified reachable; re-run `npm install` is idempotent. |\n| Lockfile records a turbo outside 2.x (impossible with `^2.5.0`, but asserted anyway) | AC 3 test also regex-checks the specifier matches `/^2\\./`; `npm ls` step confirms the resolved version. |\n| Sibling stories later add `apps/*` and change expectations | Root manifest uses only the tokens the AC names; later stories extend, not rewrite, this file. |\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] `test/package.test.cjs` exists, was written before `package.json` (RED observed first), and passes via `node --test test/` (4/4).\n- [ ] `package.json` has `name: \"nextmove\"`, `private: true`, `workspaces: [\"apps/*\"]`, `packageManager: \"npm@10\"`, `engines.node: \"22.x\"`, `devDependencies.turbo: \"^2.5.0\"`, and `turbo run build/test/lint` scripts.\n- [ ] `npm install` succeeded; `package-lock.json` generated with turbo resolving to 2.x; `node_modules/` gitignored.\n- [ ] Commit contains exactly `package.json`, `test/package.test.cjs`, `package-lock.json`, `.gitignore` — no noise files; push command executed with exit 0 (or `|| true` no-op if offline).","output":"\n\n# Implementation Plan: STORY-setup-001a — Root package.json for the NextMove monorepo\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate a minimal root `package.json` (npm workspaces, `npm@10` packageManager, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x dev dep, `turbo run` build/test/lint scripts) plus one zero-dependency `node:test` spec that asserts every acceptance criterion. TDD: write the test first (RED), add `package.json` (GREEN), install deps, then commit and push.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- AC 1: `package.json` exists — `name: \"nextmove\"`, `private: true`, `workspaces: [\"apps/*\"]`\n- AC 2: `packageManager` pinned to `npm@10`; `engines.node` specifies 22.x\n- AC 3: `devDependencies.turbo` pinned to 2.x; scripts `build`/`test`/`lint` = `turbo run build` / `turbo run test` / `turbo run lint`\n- AC 4: scaffold committed to the existing repo; git commands exit 0\n\n## Architecture Changes\n\nNone. This is a pure scaffold story — 2 new files plus a 1-line `.gitignore` append. No code, no services, no UI.\n\n## Files\n\n1. `/home/.../c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5/test/package.test.cjs` — sample unit test (created FIRST, in RED)\n2. `/home/.../c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5/package.json` — the deliverable\n3. `/home/.../c7df6267-784a-460a-addd-6d781a21b6f5/.gitignore` — append `node_modules/` and `package-lock.json`? No — append `node_modules/` only (verified: current .gitignore has neither; `node_modules/` is needed before `npm install` runs)\n\n## Decisions (explicit, with reasoning)\n\n| Decision | Choice | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| `packageManager` value | `\"npm@10\"` | AC 2 says literally \"pinned to npm@10\"; the test asserts this exact string. A fuller pin (`npm@10.9.8`) would be stricter than the AC requires and risks drifting from what later stories/orchestrator expect; keep it exactly `npm@10`. |\n| `engines.node` value | `\"22.x\"` | Satisfies \"Node 22 engines\" as the AC phrases it; installed Node is v22.23.2 so the constraint holds. |\n| Turbo specifier | `\"^2.5.0\"` | A caret on 2.x guarantees the resolved version is always 2.x (satisfies AC 3 \"pin turbo 2.x\") while allowing patch/minor updates within 2.x; verified npm registry has 2.10.11 as latest 2.x, so install will resolve within the 2.x line. |\n| Run `npm install`? | **Yes** | Registry is reachable (`npm ping PONG`); running it proves the manifest is valid, materializes the turbo dep, and generates a lockfile for reproducible builds. Workspaces glob `apps/*` matching nothing now is acceptable and expected. |\n| Commit `package-lock.json`? | **Yes** | Reproducible builds; the lockfile is part of the scaffold AC 4 asks to commit. `node_modules/` is gitignored (added to `.gitignore` in this story). |\n| Root `test` script | **Stays `turbo run test`** (per AC 3) | The sample test is deliberately NOT wired to the root `test` script — AC 3 is a hard constraint. Verification invokes it directly via `node --test test/`. This is a deliberate, documented deviation from the CLAUDE.md default \"run the project's unit test command\" since the story's AC overrides it. |\n| Test file / runner | `test/package.test.cjs`, `node --test test/` | Node 22 built-in test runner — zero added dependencies, no framework to install, `.cjs` so plain `require` works regardless of any `\"type\"` field. |\n| `.gitignore` change | Append `node_modules/` | Verified absent from the 7-line `.gitignore`; required before `npm install` creates the dir. Scoped `git add .gitignore` is used. |\n| Git add scope | `git add package.json test/ package-lock.json .gitignore` | NOT `git add -A` — must not sweep in untracked noise: `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph.log` (verified present and untracked). `.story-updates/` is orchestrator-managed and stays out of the commit. |\n\n## Implementation Steps\n\n### Phase 1 — RED (test first)\n\n**Step 1: Write the failing test**\n- Action: Create `test/package.test.cjs` with `node:test` + `node:assert/strict`. Structure:\n  - Precondition (labeled \"JSON parses\"): `require('../package.json')` inside an `assert.doesNotThrow` — or simply a first test that reads the file with `node:fs` + `JSON.parse` and asserts it is an object. This fails in RED because the file doesn't exist yet.\n  - AC 1 assertion: `pkg.name === 'nextmove'`, `pkg.private === true`, `Array.isArray(pkg.workspaces) && pkg.workspaces.includes('apps/*')`.\n  - AC 2 assertion: `pkg.packageManager === 'npm@10'`, `pkg.engines && pkg.engines.node === '22.x'`.\n  - AC 3 assertion: `pkg.devDependencies.turbo === '^2.5.0'` (and `/^2\\./.test(pkg.devDependencies.turbo)` as a belt-and-suspenders 2.x check), `pkg.scripts.build === 'turbo run build'`, `pkg.scripts.test === 'turbo run test'`, `pkg.scripts.lint === 'turbo run lint'`.\n  - Use one `test()` block per AC (4 blocks: JSON-parses, AC1, AC2, AC3) so failures are labeled 1:1 with the AC numbers in the TAP output.\n- Why: TDD — the spec must fail first; the failure mode (ENOENT / \"Cannot find module ../package.json\") proves the test actually exercises the deliverable.\n- Dependencies: none.\n- Risk: reading a missing JSON via `require` throws at load time before tests register — mitigated by doing the `fs.readFileSync` + `JSON.parse` inside the first test body (so a missing file yields a clean test failure, not a crash with zero tests run).\n- Verify: `node --test test/` → **fails** (expected RED, e.g. ENOENT for `package.json`).\n\n### Phase 2 — GREEN\n\n**Step 2: Create `package.json`**\n- Action: Write exactly:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nextmove\",\n    \"private\": true,\n    \"workspaces\": [\"apps/*\"],\n    \"packageManager\": \"npm@10\",\n    \"engines\": { \"node\": \"22.x\" },\n    \"devDependencies\": { \"turbo\": \"^2.5.0\" },\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"build\": \"turbo run build\",\n      \"test\": \"turbo run test\",\n      \"lint\": \"turbo run lint\"\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n- Why: Minimal manifest satisfying ACs 1–3 with no invented extras (no `description`/`homepage`/`type` — nothing requires them, and `\"type\": \"module\"` could break the `.cjs`-assumed test tooling in sibling stories).\n- Dependencies: Step 1.\n- Risk: none — static content.\n- Verify: `node --test test/` → **all 4 tests pass** (GREEN).\n\n**Step 3: Install dependencies and lock**\n- Action: Append `node_modules/` to `.gitignore`, then run `npm install` from the repo root.\n- Why: Validates the manifest resolves against the real registry, creates `package-lock.json`, and proves turbo 2.x resolves (lockfile will show `turbo@2.10.x`).\n- Dependencies: Step 2.\n- Risk: transient npm network failure → re-run; the story states the registry is verified reachable.\n- Verify: `npm ls turbo` → `turbo@2.10.x` (2.x line); `node --test test/` still green; `git status` shows no `node_modules/` (gitignored).\n\n### Phase 3 — Commit & push (AC 4)\n\n**Step 4: Scoped commit**\n- Action:\n  1. `git add package.json test/ package-lock.json .gitignore`\n  2. `git commit -m \"chore: add root package.json with npm workspaces, npm@10, Node 22 engines, turbo 2.x, and turbo-run scripts\"`\n  3. `git push origin HEAD 2>/dev/null || true`\n- Why: Each command must exit 0; scoped add guarantees `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph.log`, and `.story-updates/` are excluded. Push with `|| true` tolerates an offline environment per the CLAUDE.md Phase 5 convention.\n- Dependencies: Steps 2–3.\n- Risk: push rejected if remote advanced → `git pull --rebase origin iotahub/phase-1` then re-push; rebase is safe because the commit is brand-new and local-only.\n- Verify: `git status --porcelain` → only the 4 pre-existing untracked noise entries remain; `git log -1 --stat` shows exactly 4 files (`package.json`, `test/package.test.cjs`, `package-lock.json`, `.gitignore`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n- **Unit (required by gate — \"pure config, scaffold\" story):** `test/package.test.cjs` via `node --test test/`. 4 tests: JSON-parses precondition + AC 1 + AC 2 + AC 3, each labeled by AC number. Zero dependencies; no framework added.\n- **Integration / E2E:** not required — no runtime logic, no UI. Playwright explicitly out of scope per the Test Strategy Gate.\n- **Deliberate deviation (documented):** root `\"test\"` script remains `turbo run test` (AC 3), so verification invokes the sample test directly with `node --test test/` rather than `npm test`. Recorded here per the gate's deviation rule.\n\n## Verification commands (expected output)\n\n1. `node --test test/` after Step 1 → exit 1, tests fail with ENOENT (RED).\n2. `node --test test/` after Step 2 → `# pass 4` / `# fail 0` (GREEN).\n3. `npm install` → `added N packages` (N ≥ 1, includes turbo).\n4. `npm ls turbo --depth=0` → `turbo@2.10.x` (matches 2.x).\n5. `git log -1 --stat` → 4 files; `git status --porcelain` → only `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph.log` untracked (AC 4: nothing else leaked).\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Accidental commit of untracked noise via `git add -A` | Plan mandates scoped `git add` of the 4 files only; Step 4 verification greps `git status` before push. |\n| Test harness crash instead of clean RED (missing JSON at require time) | Test uses `fs.readFileSync` + `JSON.parse` inside the test body, not top-level `require`. |\n| npm registry flake during install | Registry verified reachable; re-run `npm install` is idempotent. |\n| Lockfile records a turbo outside 2.x (impossible with `^2.5.0`, but asserted anyway) | AC 3 test also regex-checks the specifier matches `/^2\\./`; `npm ls` step confirms the resolved version. |\n| Sibling stories later add `apps/*` and change expectations | Root manifest uses only the tokens the AC names; later stories extend, not rewrite, this file. |\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] `test/package.test.cjs` exists, was written before `package.json` (RED observed first), and passes via `node --test test/` (4/4).\n- [ ] `package.json` has `name: \"nextmove\"`, `private: true`, `workspaces: [\"apps/*\"]`, `packageManager: \"npm@10\"`, `engines.node: \"22.x\"`, `devDependencies.turbo: \"^2.5.0\"`, and `turbo run build/test/lint` scripts.\n- [ ] `npm install` succeeded; `package-lock.json` generated with turbo resolving to 2.x; `node_modules/` gitignored.\n- [ ] Commit contains exactly `package.json`, `test/package.test.cjs`, `package-lock.json`, `.gitignore` — no noise files; push command executed with exit 0 (or `|| true` no-op if offline).","isRawTranscript":false}}}
